# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env* is gitignored, so nothing here is committed.
#
# Required to accept a fare. Without it, /fares/review cannot accept anything and
# POST /api/fares/promote returns 403 for every request, including correct ones.
# That is intentional: an unset token means "nobody can change fares", never
# "anybody can".
#
# Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
FARE_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Optional. Only needed for the one-time network scripts, and their output is
# already committed, so a normal build never touches the network:
#   npm run data:fetch-distances   reads real stop-pair distances
#   npm run data:probe-images      checks which bus photos are still alive
